  "findings": [
    "USymbolQueue.getMargin returns Margin(5,15,5,5); asSmall translates the composed block by margin. SheetBlock1 positions each Sea at cumulative preceding height. The new first-ascent origin repair is source-backed and passes rich no-stereotype, blank-first, order/mixed-kind and boxed controls.",
    "The sequence consumer needs more precise provenance than the generic symbol alone: ComponentRoseQueue passes getTextBlock() as label and an EMPTY stereotype to USymbolQueue.asSmall. Participant.getDisplay composes the stereotype into the Display, then AbstractTextualComponent creates the complete creole block. The Rust sequence path instead gates stereo_ref and stereotype height on ParticipantLayout.in_box.",
    "Six fresh valid bare/created stereotyped queue cases remain whole failures. Their real AST contains stereotype Some(dispatch), but Rust paints zero dispatch labels versus Java two (head and tail), with missing text elements and wrong dimensions. These deficits exist before and after; they are not introduced regressions, but they disprove whole queue/stereotype composition. Existing failures do not become acceptance by correcting the ascent."
  ],
